<!doctype html>
<html lang="no">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{{ description }}">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#153863">
<meta name="app-version" content="{{ site.version }}">
{#- The programme hash above changes only when the programme does. This one
    changes when anything shipped does - templates, CSS, JS, speaker photos -
    and it is what names the service worker's cache, so it is the honest
    answer to "is this page the build the server is serving". #}
<meta name="app-build" content="{{ site.buildId }}">
<meta name="base-path" content="{{ "/" | url }}">
<link rel="manifest" href="{{ "/manifest.webmanifest" | url }}">
<link rel="icon" href="{{ "/icons/icon.svg" | url }}" type="image/svg+xml">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ "/icons/icon-180.png" | url }}">
{#- The build id on the stylesheet and script URLs is what lets a fresh page
    carry fresh assets. The worker serves these cache-first under their URL,
    so without it a page fetched past the caches (the update button, or a new
    worker's precache) would still be styled by whatever the previous worker
    had stored - and iOS Safari can keep a previous worker around for a long
    time after a deploy. A new URL is a cache miss in any worker. #}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ "/css/fonts.css" | url }}?v={{ site.buildId }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ "/css/style.css" | url }}?v={{ site.buildId }}">
{#- After the stylesheets, deliberately. A preload is fetched at the highest
    priority there is, and these fonts are not needed for the first paint at
    all - font-display: swap paints the text in a fallback immediately. Ahead
    of the render-blocking CSS they simply queued the typography in front of
    the few KB that actually gates painting, which Safari does not reorder the
    way Chrome does. Only the four weights every page uses are listed: 500 and
    italic 400 appear on one view each and can arrive late. #}
{%- for f in ["montserrat-400", "montserrat-600", "montserrat-700", "montserrat-800"] %}
<link rel="preload" href="{{ ("/css/fonts/" + f + "-latin.woff2") | url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
{%- endfor %}
<script defer src="{{ "/js/rum.js" | url }}?v={{ site.buildId }}"></script>
</head>
<body>
{{ content | safe }}

<script type="module" src="{{ "/js/app.js" | url }}?v={{ site.buildId }}"></script>
</body>
</html>
